  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Put away the strange gods, Gen. 35:2 (1 Sam. 7:3). against all the gods of Egypt I will execute judgment, Ex. 12:12. Lord is greater than all gods, Ex. 18:11. shalt have no other gods before me, Ex. 20:3 (34:14; Deut. 5:7). no mention of the name of other gods, Ex. 23:13. make us gods, which shall go before, Ex. 32:1 (Acts 7:40). shalt worship no other god, Ex. 34:14. shall serve gods, the work of men’s hands, Deut. 4:28. to go after other gods to serve them, Deut. 28:14. sacrificed … to gods whom they knew not, Deut. 32:17. Elijah said … call on the name of your gods, 1 Kgs. 18:25. Cry aloud: for he is a god, 1 Kgs. 18:27. he judgeth among the gods, Ps. 82:1. I have said, Ye are gods, Ps. 82:6 (John 10:34; D&C 76:58). Among the gods there is none like unto thee, Ps. 86:8. give thanks unto the God of gods, Ps. 136:2. cast their gods into the fire: for they were no gods, Isa. 37:19. changed their gods, which are yet no gods, Jer. 2:11. I am a God, I sit in the seat of God, Ezek. 28:2. thou hast praised the gods of silver, Dan. 5:23.",
